CSS -> Cascading Style Sheet
-------------------
|Attribute : value|
|-----------------|

Inline code example:
<html style = "background: blue"></html>

Internal code example:
<html>
     <head>
          <style>
                h1{
                  color: red;
                }
         </style>
    </head>
</html>

External code example:
 in index.html :
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./style.css"/>
 in style.css : 
  h1{
      color: green;
  }
------------------------------------------------------

. CSS selectors
  1. Class selector -> for many elements
     in index.html : <h2 class = "red-text">Red</h2>
     in style.css  : .red-text{ .. }
  2. ID selector -> for one element (both class and id can do the same but for better practicing use id for one unique element)
     in index.html : <h2 id = "red-text">Red</h2>
     in style.css  : #red-text{ .. }
  3. Attribute selector -> element + attribute condition
     in index.html : <p value="4">Red</p>
     in style.css  : p[value="4"]{ .. }
  4. Universal selector -> for all elements 
     in index.html : <h2>Red</h2>
     in style.css  : *{ .. }
------------------------------------------------------

